{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-useromd-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.58: `project-useromd`, a PROJECT-domain run whose user states a link's operating-mode distribution, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-useromd.esm`). It selects source types 21 (gasoline) and 62 (diesel), road types 1, 4 and 5, CO and Total Energy for running exhaust and THC for permeation, fuel vapor venting and fuel leaks. Its 1274 MOVESOutput rows are running exhaust on links 1 (road type 4) and 2 (road type 5), and the three evaporative processes (source type 21) on links 1, 2 and the off-network link 3.\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES, behind the input opModeDistribution (`omd_*`): the user states link 1's running distribution (thirteen round mode fractions for 201 and 9101, both source types), so LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator skips link 1 (`omd_linkRunningRows`) and BaseRateGenerator weights its running exhaust by the user's rows at every physics row of the source type (`omd_userFraction`, through `pp_W`); and the evaporative modes 150, 151 and 300 for 111, 112 and 113, which EvaporativeEmissionsOperatingModeDistributionGenerator's INSERT IGNORE keeps over its own (`evap_W` over `evap_WGenerated`). Link 2 has no user rows, so its distributions are the generators'. The pre-port model refused the run (`run_domainUnported` = 55, the user's non-start rows) and was wrong on every link-1 cell, by up to a factor of 7 on venting.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 1274. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
